Fellow extropians,

I am starting a peridoical, tentatively called META. Content will be
Wired-like, but more net oriented and more extropian. Meta will be
freely available in PostScript format. No paper edition is planned.

However, Meta will attempt to make money, through advertisers and
merchandise. As such, it is somewhat of an experiment. I do not think
any current periodical is published for profit, free to readers and
available only in an electronic edition.

Because each issue must be kept down in size (preferably under 1.4M
compressed, for obvious reasons), I would like to make Meta monthly,
although it may have to be bimonthly to start.

I envision contents along the lines of:

pages
1	cover page
1	contents/from the editor
2-4	contributing editors' observations
1-4	article/interview/story 1
1-4	article/interview/story 2 (optional)
1-2	regular/semi-regular feature 1
1-2     regular/semi-regular feature 2 (optional)
1	the end/next issue

A letters section seems superfluous in a net-based magazine, but could
be added if demanded. For the "contributing editors' observations"
section I have something in mind like a combination of the
newsbits/updates part at the beginning of many magazines and the
Reflections part of Liberty magazine, where editors can voice an
opinion or report on any news they want to. Any short reviews would
also go in this section.

The article/interview/story section is self-explanatory. I have lots of
ideas, but the only definite one is an interview with Linus Torvalds,
who has agreed to be interviewed via email. If anyone else really wants
to interview Linus, tell me asap. I would also like to get someone who
is qualified (a long time unix admin who also has used Linux
extensively) to do a review of Linux at some point.

I have two regular/semi-regular features in mind: Profiles of public
access interent providers (e.g. netcom, world) and a column in which
individuals would envision/predict/speculate on the world (any
interesting aspect thereof) in the year 2001. "Inchoate Millenium" is
the tentative title for the latter feature.

The point of this message is to find extropian editors and contributors
(I haven't asked anyone else yet). I need editors so that this does not
look quite so much like a one-person operation, and to serve as a
bogosity filter. Editors' names will be listed on or near the TOC page,
and articles sent to them before publication for comment. I will also
